# Renaming INBOX while it is selected is allowed: the session stays
# with the mailbox, which keeps its messages, uids and uidvalidity
# under the new name. The new INBOX is a different mailbox that
# happens to hold the same name, so it needs a higher uidvalidity,
# or a client would reuse a cache that no longer describes it.
send 1
f rename INBOX moved
receive 1
f OK done
send 1
f2 status INBOX (messages uidvalidity)
receive 2
* STATUS INBOX (MESSAGES 0 UIDVALIDITY 2)
f2 OK done
send 1
f3 status moved (messages uidvalidity)
receive 2
* STATUS moved (MESSAGES 1 UIDVALIDITY 1)
f3 OK done
# Both mailboxes carry on allocating UIDs from the counter the new
# INBOX inherited, so the next message in each gets UID 2. The only
# thing that keeps them apart in a client's cache is the uidvalidity,
# and this session still believes it is reading INBOX.
send 7
